// LSP M6 A1 fixture — does the EDITOR analyze the program the BUILD analyzes?
//
// Owned by tools/check-lsp.sh (and cross-checked by `kama query --symbols`, which is the point: the two
// must agree). Its kama.json declares FEATURE_A `"default": true`, so a plain build keeps `onlyWithA` and
// drops `onlyWithoutA`. Before M6 A1 the server never called setBuildFlags, so with an empty flag set it
// did the exact opposite — dropping every `@compileFor(X)` and keeping every `@compileFor(!X)`.
//
// `sources` keeps this a DECLARED project, so it is never widened by inference. Deliberately NO `main`:
// tests/query is enumerated as an inferred project by other cases, and a second `main` would collide.
// Its module is this file's FOLDER, read off the project's `modules` map (design/module-system.md §2b).

@compileFor(FEATURE_A)
fn int32 onlyWithA() { return 1; }

@compileFor(!FEATURE_A)
fn int32 onlyWithoutA() { return 0; }

fn int32 always() { return 2; }
